    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0253" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1264.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram January 27. I do not know the nature of French Minister’s new
                    instructions except by inference. The fact that the Minister had previously
                    given us a paraphrase of his instructions requiring six general advisers, and
                    has now authorized his banker to sign a letter promising advance with advisers
                    limited to service of loan, tended to confirm report that his former
                    instructions were revoked. He has not since conferred with his colleagues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
